00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.680
So when we've talking
about public data sets,

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.570
we, of course, start
at what's available?

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:28.940
What kind of public
data sets are there?

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.880
There are essentially
three different types

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.980
of public data on Google Cloud.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:35.560
The first of them
are the data sets

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:36.790
that are on Google BigQuery.

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:40.750
BigQuery is, of course, the
data warehouse in Google Cloud.

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.960
It's a good place to store
structured data sets,

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:47.020
because you can query
them using standard SQL.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.810
You get querying
up to 1 terabyte

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:51.940
per month for no charge.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.860
And to just show you the kinds
of things that are available,

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:56.140
I'll go to this website--

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:59.890
console.cloud.go
ogle.com/marketplace.

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:01.600
So I'll go into the marketplace.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.300
And you can scroll down
and you see that there

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.980
