00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:08.800
But instead of going ahead and
clicking on these data sets,

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.960
I could basically go ahead
and say, let me go ahead

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.280
and find New York City 311 data.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:19.000
So 311 in New York City is
where New Yorkers call in

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.320
with complaints--

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.070
municipal complaints.

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:26.410
So we can go there, click on
this data set, and, in addition

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:28.480
to viewing the data
set, there are a couple

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:30.770
of example queries available.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:31.630
So let's go ahead.

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:34.060
And this sounds
very interesting.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:38.500
Which New York boroughs have
the most number of parties?

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.210
If you decide to
move to New York,

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:41.720
where do you want to go live?

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:44.150
So let's go ahead
and run this query.

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:49.140
And what I'll do is I will
go ahead, wait for the query

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:50.260
to load.

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:52.610
And this is the classic UI.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:55.300
But I love the new
UI in BigQuery.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:58.180
So let me go ahead and
switch to the new UI.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:00.190
So that is the query.

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:03.160
And let me go ahead
and run the query.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:04.290
And there we go.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.330
The query basically says--

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:10.259
matter of seconds-- that
the borough is in Brooklyn,

00:02:10.259 --> 00:02:16.570
we had 110,000 or more
parties, and so on.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:19.770
And this is the different
party days, 1 being Sunday

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:20.940
and 7 being Saturday.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.220
And as you would expect,
most of the parties

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:27.010
are on Saturdays and
Sundays, although Manhattan

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:30.490
seems to have some parties
on Fridays as well.

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:32.577
So where are the
really loud parties?

00:02:32.577 --> 00:02:34.660
Well, one thing that we
did was we just went ahead

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.574
and did the query.

00:02:36.574 --> 00:02:38.240
But let's go in and
do something cooler.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:41.350
Let's go in and explore
this data in Data Studio.

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:45.310
So what this is doing is that
it's going ahead and running

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:46.840
this query for us.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.990
And I will change.

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:52.370
Right now, this is basically
based on the record count.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:55.660
So let me go ahead
and change the metric

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:57.940
to be the number of parties.

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:04.160
And instead of doing the
